## 2. Features by category


## Category: Deployment & topology

### F001 · Address space job naming (BPX.JOBNAME)

- **Category:** Deployment & topology
- **Component(s):** Common/global (zowe.*), all API ML components
- **Summary:** `ZWESVUSR` needs READ on `BPX.JOBNAME` in `FACILITY` so the z/OS UNIX address spaces of the components can be renamed (e.g. `ZWE1AG`). This is required for all components, including a stand-alone API ML install.
- **Enable / use:** RACF: `SETROPTS CLASSACT(FACILITY) RACLIST(FACILITY)`; `PERMIT BPX.JOBNAME CLASS(FACILITY) ID(ZWESVUSR) ACCESS(READ)`; `SETROPTS RACLIST(FACILITY) REFRESH`. Verify with `RLIST FACILITY BPX.JOBNAME AUTHUSER`. ZWESECUR also performs this setup.
- **Config options:**
  | Key | Alt form (env var / modulith key / property) | Default | Values / type | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | `zowe.job.prefix` | – | `ZWE1` | string | Prefix applied to component jobnames. |
  | `zowe.job.name` | – | `ZWE1SV` | string | ZWESLSTC job name. |
- **SAF / security setup:** class `FACILITY`, resource `BPX.JOBNAME`, READ, user `ZWESVUSR`.
- **Sources:** docs/user-guide/configure-zos-system.md, docs/user-guide/assign-security-permissions-to-users.md, docs/appendix/zowe-yaml-configuration.md

### F002 · API ML architecture and components (overview)

- **Category:** Deployment & topology
- **Component(s):** Gateway, Discovery Service, API Catalog, Caching Service
- **Summary:** API ML provides a single point of access for mainframe service REST APIs, with high availability, scalability, dynamic API discovery, consistent security, SSO and documentation. Overview lists four components: Gateway (secure communication, reverse proxy), Discovery Service (location/status of service instances), Catalog (UI of discovered services, APIs, Swagger docs), Caching Service (stateful key/value storage). Key features listed: consistent access (standardized service URLs), high availability, redundancy and scalability (start more service instances without config change), presentation of services (Catalog), encrypted communication, service registry with status.
- **Constraints / notes:** ⚠ Overview lists only four components and does not mention ZAAS, while api-mediation-sso.md states ZAAS (Zowe Authentication and Authorization Service) issues the SSO access token. ⚠ Overview states "The Gateway is built using Netflix Zuul and Spring Boot technology" (stated as-is). Discovery Service "is built on Eureka and Spring Boot technology".
- **Sources:** docs/user-guide/api-mediation/api-mediation-overview.md

### F003 · API ML component inventory (ports, job name suffixes, URLs)

- **Category:** Deployment & topology
- **Component(s):** Gateway, Discovery Service, API Catalog, Caching Service, ZAAS, API ML (single-service)
- **Summary:** API ML consists of five core components: API Gateway, Discovery Service, API Catalog, Caching Service, ZAAS. In single-service deployment all of them run inside one address space with job name suffix `GW`; in multi-service deployment each runs in its own address space. All Zowe servers except ZIS run under the `ZWESLSTC` started task.
- **Status / version:** Single-service deployment is "the standard and preferred method"; multi-service still supported.
- **Constraints / notes:**
  | Component | Role | Default port | Job suffix (single-service) | Job suffix (multi-service) | URL via Gateway |
  |---|---|---|---|---|---|
  | Gateway | Reverse proxy, single entry point, SSO enforcement point | 7554 (external) | `GW` | `AG` | `https://<ZOWE_HOST_ADDRESS>:7554/` (homepage) |
  | Discovery Service | Service registry (Eureka), heartbeats, routing intelligence | 7553 (external in multi-service; strictly internal in single-service) | part of `GW` | `AD` | Discovery homepage `https://<ZOWE_HOST_ADDRESS>:7553` (multi-service only) |
  | API Catalog | Web UI + REST APIs, Swagger/OpenAPI docs, try-it client | n/d in these docs (reached via Gateway 7554) | part of `GW` | `AC` | `https://<ZOWE_HOST_ADDRESS>:7554/apicatalog/ui/v1` |
  | Caching Service | Internal key-value store for HA state | 7555 (multi-service) | part of `GW` | `CS` | `https://<ZOWE_HOST_ADDRESS>:7554/cachingservice/api/v1` |
  | ZAAS | Authentication/authorization, JWT, PassTicket, PAT, identity mapping | 7558 (multi-service); 7554 in single-service (integrated in Gateway) | part of `GW` (integrated in Gateway) | n/d | n/d |
  - Ports "are dependent on each instance of Zowe and are held in the Zowe YAML configuration file".
  - Other Zowe servers routed by the Gateway: App Server/Desktop `https://<ZOWE_HOST_ADDRESS>:7554/zlux/ui/v1/` (suffix `DS1`), ZSS `https://<ZOWE_HOST_ADDRESS>:7554/zss/api/v1` (suffix `SZ`). ZIS runs as separate STC `ZWESISTC`, program `ZWESIS01`, user `ZWESIUSR`, not network accessible.
  - ⚠ Development/localhost examples in extender docs use Gateway port `10010` and Discovery port `10011` (e.g. `https://gateway:10010/ibmzosmf/...`, `https://localhost:10011/discovery/api/v1/staticApi`), not the z/OS defaults 7554/7553.
  - ⚠ ZAAS multi-service job name suffix is not documented in zowe-architecture.md.
- **Sources:** docs/getting-started/zowe-architecture.md, docs/getting-started/overview.md

### F004 · API ML component ports and jobnames (multi-service)

- **Category:** Deployment & topology
- **Component(s):** Gateway, Discovery Service, API Catalog, Caching Service, ZAAS
- **Summary:** Default TCP ports, jobnames (default prefix `ZWE1`) and log suffixes for multi-service deployment. Change them with `components.<c>.port` and `zowe.job.prefix`.
- **Status / version:** multi-service only
- **Config options:**
  | Key | Alt form (env var / modulith key / property) | Default | Values / type | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | `components.api-catalog.port` | – | `7552` | port | Jobname `ZWE1AC`, log suffix `AAC`. Views swagger/OpenAPI docs of registered services. |
  | `components.discovery.port` | – | `7553` | port or offset | Jobname `ZWE1AD`, log suffix `ADS`. Where dynamic services register and unregister. |
  | `components.gateway.port` | – | `7554` | port | Jobname `ZWE1AG`, log suffix `AGW`. Northbound edge. Must be reachable from outside z/OS (browsers, VS Code, Zowe CLI). |
