### F039 · Direct Eureka REST registration (onboarding without enabler)

- **Category:** Service discovery & onboarding
- **Component(s):** Discovery Service
- **Summary:** Any service, regardless of language, can register by sending an XML instance document to the Discovery Service's Netflix Eureka REST API, including `apiml.*` metadata keys; no enabler or Eureka client library needed. Recommended only when other methods are unsuitable.
- **Enable / use:** `POST https://{eureka_hostname}:{eureka_port}/eureka/apps/{serviceId}` with body `<instance>` containing `app`, `ipAddr`, `port enabled`, `securePort enabled`, `hostName`, `vipAddress`, `secureVipAddress`, `instanceId`, `dataCenterInfo/name` (`MyOwn`), `metadata` (flattened `apiml.*` keys). Then send heartbeats. Field details: "Service onboarding parameter reference" (EUREKA forms) and "Custom metadata reference".
- **Endpoints:**
  - `POST /eureka/apps/{serviceId}` – Discovery Service: register instance (XML body)
- **Constraints / notes:** Required parameters must be sent at registration time. Route prefix (`apiml.routes.{route-prefix}.*`) and API index (`apiml.apiInfo.{api-index}.*`) must be provided manually in XML. `vipAddress` must equal `app` and must not be omitted even if `secureVipAddress` set (Spring Cloud Netflix limitation: routes created only for instances with `vipAddress`). Alternative client libs referenced: `py-eureka-client`, `eureka-js-client`. Eureka REST operations reference: https://github.com/Netflix/eureka/wiki/Eureka-REST-operations.
- **Sources:** docs/extend/extend-apiml/onboard-direct-eureka-call.md

