### F043 · Discovery Service self-preservation threshold

- **Category:** Service discovery & onboarding
- **Component(s):** Discovery Service
- **Summary:** Eureka keeps instances in eviction status after 3 missed heartbeats plus 1 minute; when more than 15% of registered services are in eviction status, self-preservation mode prevents deregistration ("EMERGENCY! EUREKA MAY BE INCORRECTLY CLAIMING INSTANCES ARE UP…"). Exit by restarting services (3-minute spacing), restarting Discovery, or adjusting threshold.
- **Config options:**
  | Key | Alt form (env var / modulith key / property) | Default | Values / type | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | `eureka.renewalPercentThreshold` | n/d | `0.85` | decimal fraction | e.g. `0.3` = enter self-preservation when <30% not responding (as written). |
- **Sources:** docs/troubleshoot/troubleshoot-apiml.md

