- **Category:** Service discovery & onboarding
- **Component(s):** Onboarding enablers
- **Summary:** PJE builds onboarding configuration from one or two YAML files: an internal `service-configuration.yml` on the classpath (developer defaults, typically `/WEB-INF/classes`) and an optional external file anywhere on the local filesystem (sysadmin, environment-specific). Files are merged with the external file taking priority; values can be rewritten by Java system properties or servlet context parameters via `${apiml.parameter.key}` placeholders.
- **Enable / use:** Call `ApiMediationServiceConfigReader` methods: `public ApiMediationServiceConfig initializeAPIMLConfiguration(ServletContext context)` (reads file locations and `apiml.*` overrides from servlet context params); `public ApiMediationServiceConfig loadConfiguration(String configurationFileName)` (single file); `public ApiMediationServiceConfig loadConfiguration(String internalConfigurationFileName, String externalizedConfigurationFileName)` (merge). Tomcat: context XML named as the deployment unit placed in `$CATALINA_BASE/conf/[enginename]/[hostname]/`, with `<Parameter name="…" value="…"/>` entries.
- **Config options:**
  | Key | Alt form (env var / modulith key / property) | Default | Values / type | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | `apiml.config.location` | servlet context parameter | n/d | path (e.g. `/service-config.yml`) | Location of the basic (internal) configuration file. |
  | `apiml.config.additional-location` | servlet context parameter | n/d | absolute or relative path | Location of the external configuration file (higher priority). |
  | `apiml.<parameter.key>` (any other `apiml`-prefixed param) | Java system property (`-D`) or servlet context parameter | n/d | string | Rewrites the matching property value / fills `${apiml.parameter.key}` placeholders. Documented examples: `apiml.serviceId`, `apiml.serviceIpAddress`, `apiml.discoveryService.hostname`, `apiml.discoveryService.port`, `apiml.ssl.enabled`, `apiml.ssl.verifySslCertificatesOfServices`, `apiml.ssl.keyPassword`, `apiml.ssl.keystore.password`, `apiml.ssl.truststore.password`, `apiml.ssl.keystore`, `apiml.ssl.truststore` (mapped in "Service onboarding parameter reference"). |
- **Constraints / notes:** Single-file load resolution order: Java resource -> absolute file name -> relative path; then substitutes values from Java System properties. Two-file load: each file patched separately with Java System properties after loading and before merging; external takes precedence. Context-parameter key spellings for keystore/truststore use lowercase dotted forms (`apiml.ssl.keystore.password`) unlike YAML `keyStorePassword` ⚠. Example context also sets `apiml.ssl.keystore` to a `.truststore.p12` file (likely copy error ⚠).
- **Sources:** docs/extend/extend-apiml/onboard-plain-java-enabler-external-configuration.md, docs/extend/extend-apiml/onboard-plain-java-enabler.md

