### F097 · Gateway CORS handling (global)

- **Category:** CORS & HTTP handling
- **Component(s):** Gateway
- **Summary:** CORS is resolved entirely by the Gateway; backends never see CORS requests. Gateway answers preflight `OPTIONS` itself (never forwarded) and sets `Access-Control-Allow-*` headers. On actual requests it strips `Origin`, `Access-Control-Request-Method`, `Access-Control-Request-Headers` before forwarding (but Origin is preserved/forwarded by default via `apiml.security.csrf.preserveOriginForCrossSite`). When `corsEnabled: false` (default) Gateway terminates CORS itself for all paths and rejects every cross-origin request (no origins allow-listed) and ignores service overrides. When `true`, Gateway defaults apply to `/gateway/**` and per-service Custom Metadata overrides are honoured (fallback to global defaults).
- **Enable / use:** set `components.gateway.apiml.service.corsEnabled: true`; optionally set global origins/headers/methods; restart.
- **Config options:**
  | Key | Alt form (env var / modulith key / property) | Default | Values / type | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | `components.gateway.apiml.service.corsEnabled` | n/d | `false` | boolean | Enable CORS handling with per-service overrides |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.service.corsDefaultAllowedOrigins` | `apiml.service.corsDefaultAllowedOrigins` | `https://${hostname}:${port}` (Gateway's own host/port) | comma-separated origins; `*` NOT allowed | Allowed origins globally; overridable per service by `customMetadata.apiml.corsAllowedOrigins` |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.service.corsDefaultAllowedHeaders` | `apiml.service.corsDefaultAllowedHeaders` | `*` | comma-separated header list | Accepted request headers (`Access-Control-Allow-Headers`) |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.service.corsAllowedMethods` | `apiml.service.corsAllowedMethods` | `GET,HEAD,POST,PATCH,DELETE,PUT,OPTIONS` | comma-separated methods | `Access-Control-Allow-Methods` |
  | `apiml.security.csrf.preserveOriginForCrossSite` | n/d (full zowe.yaml path not given) | preserves Origin by default | boolean (implied) | Keeps and forwards the Origin header to downstream service |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.service.ignoredHeadersWhenCorsEnabled` | n/d | n/d | comma-separated list | ⚠ only in an HTML comment ("tip being validated"): override list of stripped headers; not officially documented |
- **Constraints / notes:** Default response headers: `Access-Control-Allow-Methods: GET,HEAD,POST,PATCH,DELETE,PUT,OPTIONS`, `Access-Control-Allow-Headers: *`, `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`, `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://${hostname}:${port}`. ⚠ Global property names given in short form `apiml.service.*` in one section and full `components.gateway.apiml.service.*` in others. Role: system programmer.
