### F130 · Client certificate (X.509) authentication

- **Category:** Authentication
- **Component(s):** Gateway, ZAAS
- **Summary:** Clients can authenticate with X.509 client certificates when calling a service through the Gateway or the login endpoint (exchanging the cert for a JWT). Routed flow: cert verified as valid TLS client cert against Gateway trusted CAs, checked against CA in Zowe keyring, ESM (e.g. RACF MAP) maps it to a user ID, mapped ID used for downstream authentication. Login flow: cert verified, public part verified against SAF which returns owning user ID, Gateway logs in mapped user and returns a JWT.
- **Enable / use:** Must be enabled/configured per configuration-client-certificates.md (keys not in this part). Validate: `curl -X POST --cert cert.pem --key key.pem https://<host>:<port>/gateway/api/v1/auth/login -v` -> `apimlAuthenticationToken` cookie.
- **Constraints / notes:** Basic credentials take precedence over cert on login. When calling an onboarded service endpoint, API ML ignores Basic authentication. API ML filters out its own certificates and logs them (see STC logs). Client cert must have Extended Key Usage `OID: 1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.2` (TLS client auth). Issuer certificate must be in truststore or SAF keyring. User prerequisites: with z/OSMF auth provider user ID must have a password (may be expired), NOPASSWORD/PROTECTED or suspended users cannot authenticate, PassTickets must be enabled for z/OSMF; with SAF provider no password needed for cert login/JWT generation, but password needed for PassTicket-based downstream services; suspended users cannot authenticate; user must have valid OMVS segment with unique UID. Java sample app requires JDK 17+. Default Gateway port mentioned: `7554`.
- **Sources:** docs/user-guide/authenticating-with-client-certificates.md

### F131 · Client certificate (x509) authentication and certificate-to-user mapping

- **Category:** Authentication
- **Component(s):** Gateway, ZAAS
- **Summary:** API ML can authenticate users with X.509 client certificates mapped to z/OS identities. Enable it with `x509.enabled` (through ZSS) or use the internal mapper. The external mapper URL can be customized. The STC user needs READ on `IRR.RUSERMAP`.
- **Enable / use:** `components.gateway.apiml.security.x509.enabled: true`. Optionally set `externalMapperUrl`. Keep `useInternalMapper: true` (default) for the internal mapper. Submit `ZWESECUR` for SAF, or follow the manual steps below (for upgrades from 1.18 and lower).
- **Config options:**
  | Key | Alt form (env var / modulith key / property) | Default | Values / type | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.x509.enabled` | – | n/d | boolean | Client certificate auth through ZSS. |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.x509.externalMapperUrl` | – | n/d | URL | Mapping query URL. |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.useInternalMapper` | – | `true` | boolean | Internal mapper toggle. |
- **SAF / security setup:** `FACILITY` `IRR.RUSERMAP` READ for the Gateway STC user (`ZWESVUSR`). RACF: `PERMIT IRR.RUSERMAP CLASS(FACILITY) ACCESS(READ) ID(ZWESVUSR)`; `SETROPTS RACLIST(FACILITY) REFRESH`; check with `RLIST FACILITY IRR.RUSERMAP AUTHUSER`. ACF2: `SET RESOURCE(FAC)`; `RECKEY IRR.RUSERMAP ADD(SERVICE(READ) ROLE(&STCGRP.) ALLOW)`; `F ACF2,REBUILD(FAC)`. TSS: `TSS PER(ZWESVUSR) IBMFAC(IRR.RUSERMAP) ACCESS(READ)`; check with `TSS WHOHAS IBMFAC(IRR.RUSERMAP)`. ZSS mapping also requires `BPX.SERVER` + `BPX.DAEMON` UPDATE and `OMVSAPPL` READ (see security environment switching).
- **Constraints / notes:** Required for a stand-alone API ML install that uses certificate mapping. Marked Optional in the permissions table. The certificate used for client auth must have no EKU or the `clientAuth` EKU. Password requirements differ between the z/OSMF and SAF providers.
- **Sources:** docs/appendix/zowe-yaml-configuration.md, docs/user-guide/configure-zos-system.md, docs/user-guide/assign-security-permissions-to-users.md, docs/user-guide/address-security-requirements.md, docs/user-guide/address-authentication-requirements.md

