### F144 · OIDC authentication and distributed identity mapping

- **Category:** Authentication
- **Component(s):** Gateway
- **Summary:** API ML accepts OIDC access tokens. It validates them against JWKs from one or more providers and maps the distributed identity to a z/OS user ID through a SAF registry, using the internal mapper or an external identity mapper URL. The STC user needs READ on `IRR.IDIDMAP.QUERY`, and the identity mapper user needs `IRR.RUSERMAP`.
- **Status / version:** Multiple JWKS URIs and `userIdField` since 3.4.0.
- **Enable / use:** `components.gateway.apiml.security.oidc.enabled: true`, plus `registry`, `jwks.uri` and optional `userIdField`/`identityMapperUrl`/`identityMapperUser`. Submit `ZWESECUR`, or do manual SAF setup when upgrading from 1.28 and lower.
- **Config options:**
  | Key | Alt form (env var / modulith key / property) | Default | Values / type | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.oidc.enabled` | – | n/d | boolean | Global OIDC toggle. |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.oidc.registry` | – | n/d | string | SAF registry of the distributed-identity mappings. |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.oidc.jwks.uri` | – | n/d | URI or comma-separated URIs (3.4.0+) | JWK set location(s). |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.oidc.jwks.refreshInternalHours` | – | 1 hour | hours | JWK refresh interval (key spelled `Internal`). |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.oidc.identityMapperUser` | – | `ZWESVUSR` | user ID | Identity used (via JWT) to call the mapping API. |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.oidc.userIdField` | – | `sub` | field name; dot path for nested; multi-valued fields tried in order, first successful mapping wins | Token field used for mapping (e.g. email, LDAP groups). |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.oidc.identityMapperUrl` | – | blank → internal API ML mapper; Zowe/ZSS default `https://${ZWE_haInstance_hostname}:${ZWE_components_gateway_port}/zss/api/v1/certificate/dn` | URL | Mapping API. The internal mapper is recommended since 2.14. |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.useInternalMapper` | – | `true` | boolean | Internal mapper toggle. |
- **SAF / security setup:** `FACILITY` `IRR.IDIDMAP.QUERY` READ for `ZWESVUSR`. RACF: `SETROPTS CLASSACT(IDIDMAP) RACLIST(IDIDMAP)`; `RDEFINE FACILITY IRR.IDIDMAP.QUERY`; `PERMIT IRR.IDIDMAP.QUERY CLASS(FACILITY) ACCESS(READ) ID(ZWESVUSR)`; `SETROPTS RACLIST(FACILITY) REFRESH`. ACF2: `RECKEY IRR.IDIDMAP.QUERY ADD(SERVICE(READ) ROLE(&STCGRP.) ALLOW)`; `F ACF2,REBUILD(FAC)`. TSS: `TSS PER(ZWESVUSR) IBMFAC(IRR.IDIDMAP.QUERY) ACCESS(READ)`. Identity mapper user: `FACILITY` `IRR.RUSERMAP` (set up by ZWESECUR / workflow).
- **Constraints / notes:** ACF2 requires APAR **LU01316**. The mapping (RACMAP/registry) must exist in the ESM; see ESM prerequisites in the OIDC extender doc, which is outside this part.
- **Sources:** docs/appendix/zowe-yaml-configuration.md, docs/user-guide/configure-zos-system.md, docs/user-guide/address-authentication-requirements.md, docs/user-guide/assign-security-permissions-to-users.md

### F145 · OIDC authentication – overview and flow (Identity Federation)

- **Category:** Authentication
- **Component(s):** Gateway
- **Summary:** API ML accepts access tokens issued by an external OIDC provider; with z/OS Identity Propagation this is the foundation of API ML Identity Federation. Gateway acts as OIDC client (initiates flow; access token returned to user agent in `apimlAuthenticationToken` cookie) and resource server (validates OIDC access token on requests). Valid tokens are cached; distributed identity is mapped to z/OS identity. If mapping exists, Gateway generates mainframe credentials expected by the target service (Zowe JWT, SAF IDT, or PassTicket); if no mapping, Gateway forwards the access token to the service in the `OIDC-token` header for the service to validate.
- **Constraints / notes:** Required roles: system administrator, security administrator. MFA built into OIDC provider can be used as an alternative to mainframe MFA. Prerequisites: users have SAF/ESM identity; ESM configured with distributed identity mapping; for Zowe 2.14+ Gateway must use the internal API ML mapper (default enabled since v3) or alternatively ZSS; ZSS-based authentication has a limitation with ACF2 (use internal mapper). OIDC provider: client application configured (e.g. code grant flow for server-side apps vs SPA limits) and users assigned to client app (directly or via group).
- **Sources:** docs/extend/extend-apiml/api-mediation-oidc-authentication.md; docs/user-guide/api-mediation/using-multi-factor-authentication.md

