### F154 · X.509 client certificate authentication (SSO for clients) - server-side enablement

- **Category:** Authentication
- **Component(s):** Gateway, ZAAS, z/OSMF integration
- **Summary:** Clients authenticate to API ML-onboarded APIs with X.509 client certificates mapped to SAF user IDs. Disabled by default. Mapping is done either by the Internal API ML Mapper (default/recommended in Zowe v3+, most performant, required for ACF2) or by ZSS (legacy; may be in a separate Zowe instance). Successful login via cert returns a JWT.
- **Status / version:** Internal API ML Mapper is default in Zowe v3 and later.
- **Enable / use:** set `components.gateway.apiml.security.x509.enabled: true`; keep `components.gateway.apiml.security.useInternalMapper: true` (default) or configure ZSS + `externalMapperUrl`; if z/OSMF is auth provider set `components.gateway.apiml.security.zosmf.applid`; if runtime user is not `ZWESVUSR` set `components.gateway.apiml.security.x509.externalMapperUser`; restart Zowe. Test: `curl --cert ... --key ... --cacert ... https://<gw-host>:<gw-port>/gateway/api/v1/auth/login`.
- **Config options:**
  | Key | Alt form (env var / modulith key / property) | Default | Values / type | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.x509.enabled` | n/d | disabled (feature is "disabled by default") | boolean | Global toggle for client certificate functionality |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.useInternalMapper` | n/d | `true` | boolean | Enables the Internal API ML Mapper |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.x509.externalMapperUrl` | n/d | `https://${ZWE_haInstance_hostname}:${ZWE_components_gateway_port}/zss/api/v1/certificate/x509/map` | URL | Location of API mapping certs to SAF owners (ZSS); required if ZSS is in a separate Zowe instance or ZSS hostname customized |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.x509.externalMapperUser` | n/d | n/d (skip if runtime user is default `ZWESVUSR`) | string (user ID) | Customized Zowe runtime user ID; lets Gateway generate JWTs for mapping requests |
  | `components.gateway.apiml.security.zosmf.applid` | n/d | "typically `IZUDFLT`" | string (APPLID) | z/OSMF APPLID for which API ML generates PassTickets to authenticate users to z/OSMF |
- **Endpoints:**
  `/gateway/api/v1/auth/login` – test login with client certificate, returns JWT (curl example has no `-X`; authentication-providers-for-apiml.md uses `POST` for login)
  `/zss/api/v1/certificate/x509/map` – ZSS certificate-to-SAF-user mapping API (external mapper; method n/d)
- **SAF / security setup:** Zowe runtime user (default `ZWESVUSR`) needs READ on `IRR.RUSERMAP` in class `FACILITY` (typically set by `ZWESECUR` JCL or config workflow); runtime user must be authorized for SAF identity mapping; must be member of `IZUUSER` group (z/OSMF login); must be able to generate PassTickets for the user and the z/OSMF APPLID. For ZSS mapping: runtime user must not be `NOPASSWORD` (`ALTUSER <ZOWE_RUNTIME_USER> PASSWORD(<NEWPASSWORD>)`).
- **Constraints / notes:** Truststore must contain CA (issuer) certificates of all incoming client certificates. ZSS: limitation with ACF2 (use Internal Mapper), requires certificate to be added to user in z/OS, does not support `IDMAP`. Troubleshooting: look for `X509` / `client certificate` messages in spool. ⚠ doc typos: "andshake", "sers".
- **Sources:** docs/user-guide/api-mediation/configuration-client-certificates.md

### F155 · X.509 client certificate authentication under AT-TLS (security considerations)

- **Category:** Authentication
- **Component(s):** AT-TLS, Gateway, ZAAS, Onboarding enablers
- **Summary:** Outbound AT-TLS rules configured to send the server certificate should be limited to services that require service-to-service authentication; configuration cannot be per-request, so sending the Zowe server certificate to the Gateway or to a southbound service supporting X.509 results in authenticating as the Zowe server user ID instead of the end user.
- **Constraints / notes:**
  - Use the keyring without private key for rules that must not send a client cert.
  - If an onboarded service needs X.509 client certificate authentication, use API ML integrated TLS handshake; do not configure an outbound AT-TLS rule for it.
  - Inbound `HandshakeRole ServerWithClientAuth` + `ClientAuthType Full` lets Gateway accept optional client certificates from API clients.
  - Multi-service: Gateway↔ZAAS internal calls must include X.509 client cert; single-service: internal, no AT-TLS config.
- **Sources:** docs/user-guide/configuring-at-tls-for-zowe-server.md, docs/user-guide/configuring-at-tls-for-zowe-server-single-service.md

