### F162 · JWT format and producer

- **Category:** Tokens & sessions
- **Component(s):** Gateway, ZAAS, z/OSMF integration
- **Summary:** JWT must contain unencrypted claims `sub` (z/OS user ID), `iat`, `exp`, `iss` (issuing service name), `jti`; must use RS256; signing secret is an asymmetric key generated during installation. By default, JWTs are produced by z/OSMF and API ML only serves as a proxy (provider change described in configuration-jwt.md). If z/OSMF is the authentication provider and the client already holds a z/OSMF-produced JWT, it can be reused within API ML.
