### F172 · Personal Access Token – security administrator revocation rules and eviction

- **Category:** Tokens & sessions
- **Component(s):** Gateway, Caching Service
- **Summary:** Rule-based revocation by user ID or service scope: tokens created before `timestamp` (milliseconds; default current time) are invalid; later tokens unaffected. User rules stored under `invalidUsers`, service rules under `invalidScopes`. Eviction removes expired invalidated tokens and rules related to expired tokens, to bound cache size and reduce verification cost.
- **Endpoints:** `DELETE /gateway/api/v1/auth/access-token/revoke/tokens/users` – body `{"userId":"<userId>","timestamp":"<timestamp>"}`; `204` / `401`
  `DELETE /gateway/api/v1/auth/access-token/revoke/tokens/scope` – body `{"serviceId":"<serviceId>","timestamp":"<timestamp>"}` (serviceId e.g. APPL IDs); `204` / `401`
  `DELETE /gateway/api/v1/auth/access-token/evict` – no body; `204` / `403` (lack of permissions)
- **SAF / security setup:** Administrator APIs are protected by SAF resource checking ("specific access to SAF resources"); class/resource names not given in this file.
- **Sources:** docs/user-guide/api-mediation/authenticating-with-personal-access-token.md

