### F210 · Certificate-to-user mapping: internal API ML mapper vs ZSS

- **Category:** Authorization
- **Component(s):** Gateway, ZAAS
- **Summary:** Internal API ML mapper is the default (since Zowe 3.0.0) and preferred method to map client cert public part to SAF user ID; supports both distinguished-name filter mapping (RACF `DIGTNMAP` / ACF2 & TSS `CERTMAP`) and certificate-to-user mapping. ZSS mapper only supports mapping the certificate directly to the user (cert added to user in ESM), and has a noted exception/limitation with ACF2.
- **SAF / security setup:**
  RACF (internal mapper): `SETROPTS CLASSACT(DIGTNMAP) RACLIST(DIGTNMAP)`; `RACDCERT ID(<userid>) MAP SDNFILTER('<sdn-filter>') WITHLABEL('<label>')`; `SETROPTS RACLIST(DIGTNMAP) REFRESH`.
  RACF (ZSS/cert add): `RACDCERT ADD(<dataset>) ID(<userid>) WITHLABEL('<label>') TRUST`; `SETROPTS RACLIST(DIGTCERT, DIGTRING) REFRESH`.
  ACF2 (internal mapper): `CERTMAP.<recid> SDNFILTR(<sdn-filter>) LABEL(<label>) USERID(<userid>) TRUST`; (ZSS) `INSERT <userid>.<certname> DSNAME('<dataset>') LABEL(<label>) TRUST`.
  Top Secret (internal mapper): `TSS ADDTO(<userid>) CERTMAP(<recid>) SDNFILTR('<sdn-filter>') USERID(<userid>) TRUST`; (ZSS) `TSS ADDTO(<userid>) DIGICERT(<certname>) LABLCERT('<label>') DCDSN('<dataset>') TRUST`.
  SDN check commands: RACF `RACDCERT CHECKCERT('dsn')`; ACF2 `SET PROFILE(USER) DIV(CERTDATA)` + `CHKCERT DSN('dsn')`; TSS `TSS CHKCERT DCDSN('dsn')`.
- **Constraints / notes:** SDNFILTER (SDNFILTR in ACF2/TSS) must exactly match casing, spacing and order of the ESM CHECKCERT display (e.g. `CN=USER1.OU=DEPT1.O=ORG1`). Map commands avoid adding the cert to the ESM database; considered more convenient but possibly less secure than adding cert to the ACID. The setting to disable the internal mapper is not given in this part.
- **Sources:** docs/user-guide/authenticating-with-client-certificates.md; docs/extend/extend-apiml/api-mediation-oidc-authentication.md

