### F224 · Security environment switching (impersonation) for ZSS-based mapping

- **Category:** Authorization
- **Component(s):** Common/global (zowe.*), Gateway (via ZSS)
- **Summary:** `ZWESVUSR` needs UPDATE on `BPX.SERVER` and `BPX.DAEMON` to act under the logged-on user's identity. All Zowe users, plus the STC user, need READ on `OMVSAPPL` in `APPL` when that profile is defined. Listed as required for ZSS, which API ML certificate and identity mapping depend on. Required for a stand-alone API ML install.
- **SAF / security setup:** RACF: `RDEFINE FACILITY BPX.SERVER UACC(NONE)`; `RDEFINE FACILITY BPX.DAEMON UACC(NONE)`; `PERMIT BPX.SERVER CLASS(FACILITY) ID(ZWESVUSR) ACCESS(UPDATE)`; `PERMIT BPX.DAEMON CLASS(FACILITY) ID(ZWESVUSR) ACCESS(UPDATE)`; `SETROPTS RACLIST(FACILITY) REFRESH`. TSS: `TSS PERMIT(ZWESVUSR) IBMFAC(BPX.SERVER) ACCESS(UPDATE)` (same for `BPX.DAEMON`). ACF2: `RECKEY BPX ADD(SERVER ROLE(ZWESVUSR) SERVICE(UPDATE) ALLOW)` (same for `DAEMON`). OMVSAPPL: RACF `PERMIT OMVSAPPL CLASS(APPL) ID(<zowe_user>) ACCESS(READ)`; TSS `TSS PERMIT(<zowe_user>) APPL(OMVSAPPL)`; ACF2 `RECKEY OMVSAPPL ADD(SERVICE(READ) ROLE(<zowe_user>) ALLOW)`.
- **Constraints / notes:** Skip the OMVSAPPL step when the profile is undefined. ⚠ The ACF2 check command says `LIST OMVSAAPL` (typo).
- **Sources:** docs/user-guide/configure-zos-system.md, docs/user-guide/assign-security-permissions-to-users.md, docs/user-guide/address-security-requirements.md

