### F231 · AT-TLS enablement for Zowe servers (zowe.network AT-TLS-aware mode)

- **Category:** Certificates & TLS
- **Component(s):** AT-TLS, Common/global (zowe.*), Gateway, Discovery Service, API Catalog, Caching Service, ZAAS, API ML (single-service)
- **Summary:** Zowe server components can switch from built-in (native) TLS to AT-TLS so that TLS is offloaded to z/OS Communications Server (PAGENT policy). Inbound and outbound AT-TLS awareness are enabled separately. Even with AT-TLS, API ML needs information about the server certificate defined in the AT-TLS rule, so those server certificates must be trusted in the Zowe keyring configured in `zowe.yaml`.
- **Status / version:** native TLS is the default. Client (outbound) AT-TLS setting supported since 3.1.0 (v3_1_0 release note #3828).
- **Enable / use:** set `zowe.network.server.tls.attls: true` (inbound rules) and, if outbound rules are configured, `zowe.network.client.tls.attls: true`; define PAGENT rules; `F PAGENT,REFRESH`; restart Zowe.
- **Config options:**
  | Key | Alt form (env var / modulith key / property) | Default | Values / type | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | `zowe.network.server.tls.attls` | n/d | `false` (shown in v2.16 upgrade snippet) | boolean | Enables AT-TLS-aware mode for inbound traffic. |
  | `zowe.network.client.tls.attls` | n/d | `false` (shown in v2.16 upgrade snippet) | boolean | Enables AT-TLS-aware mode for outbound traffic; when `true`, AT-TLS performs encryption even when requests are issued as `http`. |
  | `zowe.network.server.tls.minTls` | n/d | `"TLSv1.2"` (upgrade snippet) | TLS version string | Native TLS min version; "TLS settings only apply when attls=false". Must NOT be set together with `attls: true`. |
  | `zowe.network.server.tls.maxTls` | n/d | `"TLSv1.3"` (upgrade snippet) | TLS version string | Native TLS max version; must NOT be set together with `attls: true`. |
  | `zOSMF.scheme` | n/d | n/d | `https` | Required when `zowe.network.client.tls.attls: true` and no z/OSMF outbound rule exists in PAGENT. |
- **Constraints / notes:**
  - "Do not set `attls: true` together with `minTls` or `maxTls`. Zowe does not handle TLS in AT-TLS aware mode."
  - Other components that talk to the Gateway (e.g. Zowe App Server) also require AT-TLS configuration.
  - Recommend restarting Zowe services after refreshing PAGENT (open connections).
  - Inline comments in sample rules must be removed in the real z/OS configuration (may be read by the interpreter).
  - Security administrator role. Beginning v3.4.0, single-service deployment mode is recommended (separate article).
  - ⚠ v3_5_0 release notes: zlux fixes show component-level overrides `components.app-server.zowe.network.client.tls.attls` and `components.app-server.zowe.network.server.tls.attls` (app-server only).
- **Sources:** docs/user-guide/configuring-at-tls-for-zowe-server.md, docs/user-guide/configuring-at-tls-for-zowe-server-single-service.md, docs/upgrade/upgrading-zowe-v3.md, docs/upgrade/upgrade-zowe-v3.md, docs/whats-new/release-notes/v3_1_0.md, docs/whats-new/release-notes/v3_5_0.md

