### F257 · Keystore and truststore configuration (PKCS12 and z/OS keyring)

- **Category:** Certificates & TLS
- **Component(s):** Common/global (zowe.*), all API ML components
- **Summary:** `zowe.certificate` sets the keystore (server certificate) and truststore (CAs) for all components. It can be file-based PKCS12, recommended for proof of concept, or a z/OS keyring (`safkeyring://owner/ring`), recommended for production because access is controlled by SAF privileges rather than passwords. A PEM triplet can be given for apps that support neither format.
- **Enable / use:** PKCS12: `type: PKCS12`, `file`, `password`, `alias` for the keystore, plus a truststore (can be separate) and a `pem` section. Keyring: `type: JCERACFKS` (or another JCE type), `file: safkeyring://YOURID/YOURKEYRING`, `password: password` (literal), and `alias` = case- and space-sensitive label. The truststore can reference the keystore values with templates (`"${{ zowe.certificate.keystore.type }}"` etc.). Remove `zowe.certificate.pem` for keyrings. If you used `zwe init certificate --update-config`, this section is filled in automatically.
- **Config options:**
  | Key | Alt form (env var / modulith key / property) | Default | Values / type | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | `zowe.certificate.keystore.type` | – | n/d | `PKCS12`; `JCERACFKS` (keyring default), `JCECCARACFKS`, `JCEHYBRIDRACFKS`; API ML also `JCEKS`, `JCECCAKS` | Keystore type. |
  | `zowe.certificate.keystore.file` | – | n/d | path / `safkeyring://<owner>/<ring>` | Keystore. |
  | `zowe.certificate.keystore.password` | – | n/d | string / literal `password` for keyrings | Password. |
  | `zowe.certificate.keystore.alias` | – | n/d | alias / keyring label | Server certificate. |
  | `zowe.certificate.truststore.type` | – | n/d | as keystore | Truststore type. |
  | `zowe.certificate.truststore.file` | – | n/d | path / safkeyring URL | Truststore. |
  | `zowe.certificate.truststore.password` | – | n/d | string | Password. |
  | `zowe.certificate.pem.key` | – | n/d | PEM path | Private key. |
  | `zowe.certificate.pem.certificate` | – | n/d | PEM path | Certificate. |
  | `zowe.certificate.pem.certificateAuthorities` | – | n/d | PEM path | CAs. |
- **Constraints / notes:** All files must be readable by the Zowe runtime user, and the keyring must be accessible to it. Zowe startup re-verifies the configuration. For ICSF hardware private keys, use `JCEHYBRIDRACFKS`. With AT-TLS, the keyring in the AT-TLS policy should be the same as in `zowe.certificate`. ⚠ The appendix lists only `JCEHYBRIDRACFKS`/`JCECCARACFKS`/`JCERACFKS` for keyrings. The finalize doc adds `JCEKS`/`JCECCAKS` for API ML. certificate-analyser accepts only `PKCS12`/`JCERACFKS`/`JCECCARACFKS`/`JCEHYBRIDRACFKS`.
- **Sources:** docs/appendix/zowe-yaml-configuration.md, docs/user-guide/configure-certificates.md, docs/user-guide/certificates-finalize-configuration.md

