  | Key | Alt form | Default | Values / type | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | `components.api-catalog.enabled` | – | n/d | boolean | Set to `false` on the instance that does not run UI services, so only one API Catalog is active across maintenance levels. |
  | `zowe.setup.datasets`, `zowe.setup.security`, `zowe.runtimeDirectory`, `zowe.logDirectory`, `zowe.workspaceDirectory`, `zowe.job` | – | n/d | – | Must differ between the two instances. All other settings, including HA and security, must match. |
- **SAF / security setup:** `CONTROL` access to `MVS.VARY.TCPIP.SYSPLEX` to run the `VARY` command.
- **Constraints / notes:** Only one API Catalog instance can be active when instances run different maintenance levels. Onboarded services must also be in HA mode. Long-lived connections (long-running requests, WebSocket sessions) cannot be re-routed and close when the instance stops. Assumes a single shared zFS, two instances (A, B) on the same version, and a Sysplex Distributor.
- **Sources:** `docs/upgrade/upgrade-zowe-no-downtime.md`


