### F389 · Gateway REST API OpenAPI definition (inventory)

- **Category:** Other
- **Component(s):** Gateway
- **Summary:** OpenAPI 3.0.0 spec "API Gateway" version 1.3.0, server URL `/gateway`, tags Security, Services, Diagnostic. Security schemes: `LoginBasicAuth` (http basic), `Bearer` (http bearer, format JWT), `CookieAuth` (apiKey in cookie `apimlAuthenticationToken`).
- **Endpoints:** `POST /auth/login` – login (LoginBasicAuth / JSON body / client cert) -> 204 + cookie
  `GET /auth/query` – validate token (Cookie/Bearer) -> 200 Authentication
  `POST /auth/ticket` – generate PassTicket (Cookie/Bearer + client cert) -> 200 TicketResponse
  `POST /auth/refresh` – refresh JWT (Cookie/Bearer + client cert; disabled by default) -> 204 + cookie
  `POST /auth/logout` – invalidate session (Cookie/Bearer) -> 204
  `GET /version` – version info (no auth declared) -> 200 VersionInfo
  `GET /auth/keys/public/all` – all JWKs (Cookie/Bearer) -> 200 JWKSet
  `GET /auth/keys/public/current` – current JWKs (Cookie/Bearer) -> 200 JWKSet
  `GET /services` – all services, query param `apiId` (optional, string, e.g. `zowe.apiml.gateway`) (Cookie/Bearer; SAF `APIML.SERVICES`/`ZOWE` READ) -> 200 array ServiceInfo + header `Content-version`
  `GET /services/{serviceId}` – one service, path param `serviceId` (required) -> 200 ServiceInfo + `Content-version` / 404 service does not exist / 500
- **Constraints / notes:** ⚠ Spec does not include PAT endpoints (`/auth/access-token/*`), OIDC validate (`/auth/oidc-token/validate`), `/registry`, or `/certificates`, which are documented in user docs. ⚠ Server `/gateway` + paths gives `/gateway/auth/...` while user docs use `/gateway/api/v1/auth/...`.
- **Sources:** api_definitions/gateway.json

