### F395 · Custom metadata reference

- **Category:** Service discovery & onboarding
- **Component(s):** Onboarding enablers, Gateway, Discovery Service, ZAAS client
- **Summary:** Additional metadata added under `customMetadata` is registered in the Discovery Service and propagated to onboarded services (clients). Arbitrary metadata does not change client behavior; `apiml.`-prefixed keys configure API ML (Gateway) behavior per service. Define your own qualifier for non-API ML metadata.
- **Enable / use:** PJE/STATIC: `customMetadata: { apiml: { <key>: <value> } }` (or `customMetadata.apiml.<key>`). Spring enabler: prefix with `apiml.service` -> `apiml.service.customMetadata.apiml.<key>` (documented explicitly for the first 12 rows below, enableUrlEncodedCharacters through corsAllowedMethods; for the remaining rows by the general rule). Direct Eureka XML: flattened `<apiml.<key>>` in `<metadata>` where documented.
- **Config options:**
  | Key | Alt form (env var / modulith key / property) | Default | Values / type | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | `customMetadata.apiml.enableUrlEncodedCharacters` | SB `apiml.service.customMetadata.apiml.enableUrlEncodedCharacters`; SB top-level `apiml.enableUrlEncodedCharacters`; EUREKA `apiml.enableUrlEncodedCharacters` | `true` (recommended) | boolean | Gateway allows encoded characters in URL requests routed to the service; set `false` only to reject certain encoded characters. For encoded slash/backslash (`%2F`, `%5C`) the Gateway must also be configured to allow encoded slashes. ⚠ EUREKA XML sample sets `false`. |
  | `customMetadata.apiml.connectTimeout` | SB `apiml.service.customMetadata.apiml.connectTimeout`; EUREKA `apiml.connectTimeout` | Gateway service configuration value | ms | Period to establish a single non-managed connection with this service. |
  | `customMetadata.apiml.readTimeout` | SB `apiml.service.customMetadata.apiml.readTimeout`; EUREKA `apiml.readTimeout` | Gateway service configuration value | ms | Max inactivity between two packets in response from the service. |
  | `customMetadata.apiml.connectionManagerTimeout` | SB `apiml.service.customMetadata.apiml.connectionManagerTimeout`; EUREKA `apiml.connectionManagerTimeout` | Gateway service configuration value | ms | Period in which managed connections (HTTP connection manager) with API ML are established. |
  | `customMetadata.apiml.okToRetryOnAllOperations` | SB `apiml.service.customMetadata.apiml.okToRetryOnAllOperations`; EUREKA `apiml.okToRetryOnAllOperations` | `false` | boolean | `false`: only `GET` retried on `503`. `true`: all methods retried on `503` (request body buffering may impact resources). |
  | `customMetadata.apiml.corsEnabled` | SB `apiml.service.customMetadata.apiml.corsEnabled`; EUREKA doc lists `apiml.service.corsEnabled` ⚠ | n/d | boolean | Enables Gateway CORS handling on service level for all service routes. |
  | `customMetadata.apiml.gatewayAuthEndpoint` | SB `apiml.service.customMetadata.apiml.gatewayAuthEndpoint` | `/api/v1/gateway/auth` | path | Gateway authentication endpoint used by ZAAS Client configuration. |
  | `customMetadata.apiml.gatewayPort` | SB `apiml.service.customMetadata.apiml.gatewayPort` | `10010` | port | Gateway port used by ZAAS Client configuration. |
  | `customMetadata.apiml.corsAllowedOrigins` | SB `apiml.service.customMetadata.apiml.corsAllowedOrigins`; EUREKA doc lists `customMetadata.apiml.corsAllowedOrigins` | falls back to Gateway `corsDefaultAllowedOrigins` (`https://${hostname}:${port}`) | comma-separated origins | Optional. Origins accepted by Gateway during CORS handling for this service; additive to Gateway defaults (does not replace). |
  | `customMetadata.apiml.corsAllowedHeaders` | SB `apiml.service.customMetadata.apiml.corsAllowedHeaders`; EUREKA doc same key | n/d | comma-separated header names | Optional. Headers allowed in CORS requests to the service. |
  | `customMetadata.apiml.corsAllowCredentials` | SB `apiml.service.customMetadata.apiml.corsAllowCredentials`; EUREKA doc same key | `true` (Gateway-level and per-service default) | boolean | Optional. Whether browser includes credentials (cookies, authorization headers, TLS client certs) in CORS requests. |
  | `customMetadata.apiml.corsAllowedMethods` | SB `apiml.service.customMetadata.apiml.corsAllowedMethods`; EUREKA doc same key | n/d | comma-separated methods (e.g. `GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `DELETE`) | Optional. HTTP methods allowed via CORS. |
  | `customMetadata.apiml.lb.type` | SB (general rule) `apiml.service.customMetadata.apiml.lb.type` | unset = basic round robin | `headerRequest`, `authentication` | Deterministic routing load-balancing schema (see the two Deterministic routing features). |
