### F396 · Keyring reference and password requirements in v3

- **Category:** Certificates & TLS
- **Component(s):** Common/global (zowe.*)
- **Summary:** Keyring URLs must use `safkeyring://` (two slashes; `safkeyring:////` no longer accepted). v3 requires keystore and truststore password set to the literal `password` for keyring-based certificates (v2 accepted empty).
- **Status / version:** breaking in 3.0.0.
- **Config options:**
  | Key | Alt form (env var / modulith key / property) | Default | Values / type | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|---|
  | `zowe.certificate.keystore.file` | n/d | n/d | `safkeyring://<owner>/<ring>` | e.g. `safkeyring://ZWESVUSR/ZoweKeyring`. |
  | `zowe.certificate.keystore.type` | n/d | n/d | `JCERACFKS` (sample) | Keyring type. |
  | `zowe.certificate.keystore.password` | n/d | n/d | literal `password` | Required for keyrings in v3. |
  | `zowe.certificate.keystore.alias` | n/d | n/d | label (sample `localhost`) | Certificate alias. |
  | `zowe.certificate.truststore.file` / `type` / `password` | n/d | n/d | as above; password literal `password` | Truststore. |
- **Sources:** docs/upgrade/upgrading-zowe-v3.md, docs/upgrade/upgrade-zowe-v3.md, docs/whats-new/breaking-changes-v3.md, docs/whats-new/release-notes/v3_0_0.md

